
=== Does the white-balance lock reach the die, and does it hold? (#30, #33) ===

clock     : 320 MHz sys
sensor id : 0x82

-- bring-up --
  sensor id : 0x82  (legacy table)
  firmware  : 2023-03-03, fpga rev 32

-- warm-up, auto loops running --
  settled at luma 133

-- placing the ladder against this scene --
  the die's own AE, loop free and settled: 0x024c
  written        8     10     20     40     80    100    200    400    800   1000   2000   4000   8000  10000
  die says   024c?  024c?  024c?  024c?  024c?  024c?  024c?  0400   0800   024c?  024c?  024c?  024c?  0000 
  3 of 14 echoed the write; ? marks the ones that did not and are ignored
  0x00400 lands the die nearest its own choice (off by 436), so the ladder is 80 100 200 400 800 1000

-- does a lock reach the die? asked at 0x3002/0x3003, not at the picture --
  locked         wrote 0080, die: 0080 0080 0080 0080 0080 0080 0080 0080 0080 0080   held
  locked         wrote 0400, die: 0400 0400 0400 0400 0400 0400 0400 0400 0400 0400   held
  AE free        wrote 0080, die: 0080 0080 0080 0080 0080 0080 0080 0080 0080 0080   held
  locked held both exposures:  yes
  AE free dragged it back:     no   <- the control failed, so nothing here is readable
  -> INCONCLUSIVE: the die held the write even with AE free, so this stage
     cannot tell a lock from a loop that had nowhere to go.

-- stage M: sweep 1024 addresses from 0x3000, every loop free against every loop locked --
